infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Fixing TIME-WAIT exhaustion — in that order
  desc EADDRNOTAVAIL on connect(): stopgaps first, structural fix last
  order asc
  sequences
    - label tcp_tw_reuse=1 — safe timestamp-based reuse
      desc Reuses a TIME-WAIT entry for a new outbound connection only when Timestamps prove the SYN is newer (RFC 6191). No data-corruption risk. Never tcp_tw_recycle — removed in 4.12 for breaking NAT.
    - label Widen ip_local_port_range to 1024 65535
      desc Default ~28k ephemeral ports (32768-60999) becomes ~64k. Buys headroom against the ~120s (2xMSL) TIME-WAIT lifetime, but does not stop burning a four-tuple per request.
    - label Connection pool with keep-alive — the real fix
      desc Each upstream connection serves many requests, so the LB stops opening a fresh four-tuple per request. TIME-WAIT stops accumulating and the problem disappears entirely.
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b #10b981
